{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers","id":1168101,"title":"[2E] Fixing Dread Powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-15T19:38:45-08:00","id":1168101,"title":"[2E] Fixing Dread Powers","content":"<b>WtF</b> 2E is highly based on Dread Powers of various Preys. I found some of their mechanics to be too much or too little compared to Uratha capabilities. Here is topic for finding those and talking over them.<br /> <br /> 1. <b><i>Colossus</i> Dread Power</b> - Generally, it's great package of rules for 'giant, massive monster' to use for your making your enemies. However, the problem is with it's 'gains general Armor equal to its Resistance' part - as most beings having Colossus in first place would naturally have Resistance over 5 ( they are COLOSSUS, in the end ) - so it makes being practically 'unhittable' with anything that is non-Bane. I found that much better is give beings general Armor equal to Rank, rather. It's then still hard to opposed most attacks - but not making being immune to anything less than granade launcher. Most those beings still be Rank 3-4, so they will still damn powerful to oppose most weapons damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T20:09:53-08:00","id":1168106,"title":"","content":"Well, wasn\u2019t \u201cunhittable by anything but its Bane\u201d the intended effect?<br /> <br /> <br /> A question of my own; how does everyone deal with the almost-identical Dread Powers between CofD core and Werewolf? Does the latter override the former, or are they separate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:07:39-08:00","id":1168112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers#post1168101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Colossus</i> Dread Power</b> - Generally, it's great package of rules for 'giant, massive monster' to use for your making your enemies. However, the problem is with it's 'gains general Armor equal to its Resistance' part - as most beings having Colossus in first place would naturally have Resistance over 5 ( they are COLOSSUS, in the end ) - so it makes being practically 'unhittable' with anything that is non-Bane.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a game with a core Merit whose effects start with giving one of your form's natural weapons AP2, advances to giving that same weapon an extra point of damage, and caps with blanket negation of non-magical armor.<br /> <br /> This is <i>also</i> a game where the Dread Power you're talking about is part of a list of abilities demonstrated by the powerful out-of-context problem antagonists for which the gameline's Chronicle is named, whose predominant issues include &quot;figuring out this thing's weaknesses is difficult and may require you to investigate the beings it creates before you even begin to set about the process of finding the highly specific bane of a Rank 4-5 spiritual being.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm going to put forward the notion that this is a feature, not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:08:58-08:00","id":1168113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168106#post1168106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, wasn\u2019t \u201cunhittable by anything but its Bane\u201d the intended effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Should it? With Colossus beings - they will have <i>really</i> high Resistance levels, just from conceptual level. Add to it rather large Size, doubled Corpus bonus from Resistance ( it's in Dread Power Description ) and we <b>easily</b> are beyond 20 Corpus, often in levels of 50+. Add to it \u201cunhittable by anything but its Bane\u201d and we look over things that even when NOT BIGGEST AND MONSTROUS in the world - i.e. Size 20-30, like a plane - and we end with thing that PCs cannot do <i>any</i> damage. Like even levels of 1-2 Lethals on Corpus 50. It's simply too much. I can understand 'we hit it with rocket launcher and it was to it like swing of baseball bat' ( i.e. Lethal 1-3 ), but reducing <b>any damage PCs can make</b> ( remember, we talk here about high Resistance beings, so Armor like 5+ ) to 1 Bashing on Corpus 50 levels is just <i>insanely</i> demotivating to players.<br /> <br /> Compare to my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-\u2013-dragon-idigam?p=1138235#post1138235\">Fear of Scales Rank 4 being</a> - this ancient Pangean-like Norse Dragon that has 'typical' Corpus of circa of 58 boxes. Add to it it's Resistance as Armor - i.e. 10 points - and PCs need to hit it like 30 times by 11+ to even go it to half of it's Health track to make it retreat. Without some sort divine intervention, PCs are powerless to do it ANYTHING without Bane.<br /> <br /> I'm all into making Bane the easiest way to kill being - but some damage should be possible to get it normally, even to stop by being in looking for proper solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-16-2017, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:18:50-08:00","id":1168115,"title":"","content":"It really seems like with Colossus it would depend completely on the group and situation, and otherwise it's doing what it's supposed to.<br /> <br /> You don't just tack on a Dread Power because it sounds cool. You have your players character sheets, you have likely seen them in combat, you should know how much damage they are capable of doing. Moreover, the Colossus Dread Power is originally for idigam. It is for a chronicle-spanning threat that can conceivably take multiple packs to fight.<br /> <br /> By all means, lower it for your own game or excise it completely. There's no reason to think that should be the case for everyone's game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:28:16-08:00","id":1168118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168112#post1168112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a game with a core Merit whose effects start with giving one of your form's natural weapons AP2, advances to giving that same weapon an extra point of damage, and caps with blanket negation of non-magical armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you point those to me in 2E corebook? I did miss those info to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:38:51-08:00","id":1168120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168118#post1168118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you point those to me in 2E corebook? I did miss those info to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Living Weapon, the third of the three core Merits that let you boost specific forms alongside Fortified Form and Favored Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:40:05-08:00","id":1168121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168113#post1168113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should it? With Colossus beings - they will have <i>really</i> high Stamina levels, just from conceptual level. Add to it rather large Size, doubled Corpus bonus from Resistance ( it's in Dread Power descripton ) and we <b>easily</b> are beyond 20 Corpus, often in levels of 50+. Add to it \u201cunhittable by anything but its Bane\u201d and we look over things that even when NOT BIGGEST AND MONSTEROUS in the world - i.e. Size 20-30, like a plane - and we end with thing that PCs cannot do <i>any</i> damage. Like even levels of 1-2 Lethals on Corpus 50. It's simply too much. I can understand 'we hit it with rocket launcher and it was to it like swing of baseball bat' ( i.e. Lethal 1-3 ), but reducing <b>any damage PCs can make</b> ( remember, we talk here about high Resistance beings, so Armor like 5+ ) to 1 Bashing on Corpus 50 levels is just <i>insanely</i> demotivating to players.<br /> <br /> Compare to my <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-\u2013-dragon-idigam?p=1138235#post1138235&amp;quot;]Fear</a> of Scales Rank 4 being[/URL] - this ancient Pangean-like Norse Dragon that has 'typical' Corpus of circa of 58 boxes. Add to it it's Resistance as Armor - 10 points - and PCs need to hit it like 30 times by 11+ to even go it to half of it's Health track to make it retreat. Without some sort divine intervention, PCs are powerless to do it ANYTHING without Bane.<br /> <br /> I'm all into making Bane the easiest way to kill being - but some damage should be possible to get it normally, even to stop by being in looking for proper solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t complain when I can\u2019t demolish a building with my barehands; I bring explosives and experienced personnel. When lions hunt an elephant, they don\u2019t charge at it from the front in a glorious blaze of battle; they wait until it is weakened, distract its kin away so that is isolated, harry it to tire it, and only then move in for the kill. <br /> <br /> Similar logic here. If a prey can\u2019t be brought down by claws and fangs, perhaps more esoteric means are required after all. Certainly the apex predators of Flesh and Shadow are smart enough to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T21:53:29-08:00","id":1168123,"title":"","content":"While on the subject of Dread Powers; can a creature take the Numen Dread Power to gain access to angelic Numina? Should it be banned? It\u2019s a thought that came to me after rereading the (unofficial) stats for Lycaon-Ur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T22:16:17-08:00","id":1168126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168123#post1168123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While on the subject of Dread Powers; can a creature take the Numen Dread Power to gain access to angelic Numina? Should it be banned? It\u2019s a thought that came to me after rereading the (unofficial) stats for Lycaon-Ur.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does he have any Numina?<br /> <br /> I don't see why it should be banned. Maybe a little rare, but you do have things like spirits that might have worked closely with or devoured angels. Plus considering there's spirits of basically everything you're bound to have some overlap in capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T22:25:23-08:00","id":1168128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168126#post1168126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does he have any Numina?<br /> <br /> I don't see why it should be banned. Maybe a little rare, but you do have things like spirits that might have worked closely with or devoured angels. Plus considering there's spirits of basically everything you're bound to have some overlap in capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Lycaon-Ur himself; his writeup inspired me about spirits interacting with angels, with the writeup heavily implying that Lycaon-Ur\u2019s transformation had to do with them.<br /> <br /> And your advice is sound. Back to the tinkering lab, it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T23:41:55-08:00","id":1168134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers#post1168101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>WtF</b> 2E is highly based on Dread Powers of various Preys. I found some of their mechanics to be too much or too little compared to Uratha capabilities. Here is topic for finding those and talking over them.<br /> <br /> 1. <b><i>Colossus</i> Dread Power</b> - Generally, it's great package of rules for 'giant, massive monster' to use for your making your enemies. However, the problem is with it's 'gains general Armor equal to its Resistance' part - as most beings having Colossus in first place would naturally have Resistance over 5 ( they are COLOSSUS, in the end ) - so it makes being practically 'unhittable' with anything that is non-Bane. I found that much better is give beings general Armor equal to Rank, rather. It's then still hard to opposed most attacks - but not making being immune to anything less than granade launcher. Most those beings still be Rank 3-4, so they will still damn powerful to oppose most weapons damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like it the way it is since it gives trouble to the PCs, it makes them think with the mind instead of their muscles and I love it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T03:26:52-08:00","id":1168148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168123#post1168123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While on the subject of Dread Powers; can a creature take the Numen Dread Power to gain access to angelic Numina? Should it be banned? It\u2019s a thought that came to me after rereading the (unofficial) stats for Lycaon-Ur.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's going to have to be an ST call. Now, in general, the assumption here is that werewolf critters are going to have spirit-based numina. But if its appropriate for an antagonist to have something like this, then sure, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T08:45:49-08:00","id":1168197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168120#post1168120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Living Weapon, the third of the three core Merits that let you boost specific forms alongside Fortified Form and Favored Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so if I take Living Weapon and maxed out it for Gauru claws they will have bypass 2 Armor of Colossus being, they will do +3 Damage - so it's will 'bypass' Armor 5 on hit, is it? Or will Living Weapon ***** let you automaticly bypass even Armor 10+ in Colossus beings?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168121#post1168121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t complain when I can\u2019t demolish a building with my barehands; I bring explosives and experienced personnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is before modern times - I run a Viking Era <b>WtF</b> game ( year 800 A.D. ) and I cannot envision things making this more than +5 Damage that are not some 'ancient artifact of great power' to even <i>scratch</i> Colossus being with RAW. On last game session players used <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1157475-dark-eras-how-to-run-war-machines?p=1157477#post1157477\">Balista made with +4 Damage</a> and +5 bonus from Planing action - but still got only a 6 Lethal on shooting being with it, so even with my lowered Armor to Idigam Rank ( 4 in Coaleseed Form ) they only made it 2 Lethal. Out of Corpus 70 of it. So it's hitting by Balista, fully prepared, is like stabbing by toothpick on normal person. On <i>lowered</i> by my the Armor on Colossal Idigam.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168121#post1168121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When lions hunt an elephant, they don\u2019t charge at it from the front in a glorious blaze of battle; they wait until it is weakened, distract its kin away so that is isolated, harry it to tire it, and only then move in for the kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>HOW can you make something weakened that any non-modern Weapon of Massive Distraction is like toothpick for it? Finding 'the one and only Bane' for Rank 4-5 being is not very much an answer when it's destroying your village. You need at least to weakened it so you can have time to look for proper Bane for it. Do SOMETHING before finding one and final solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:05:26-08:00","id":1168211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168112#post1168112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a game with a core Merit whose effects start with giving one of your form's natural weapons AP2, advances to giving that same weapon an extra point of damage, and caps with blanket negation of non-magical armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lets not forget Shaping gift Facet (Glory) which gives you glory\u00b4s in armor piercing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers#post1168101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>WtF</b> 2E is highly based on Dread Powers of various Preys. I found some of their mechanics to be too much or too little compared to Uratha capabilities. Here is topic for finding those and talking over them.<br /> <br /> 1. <b><i>Colossus</i> Dread Power</b> - Generally, it's great package of rules for 'giant, massive monster' to use for your making your enemies. However, the problem is with it's 'gains general Armor equal to its Resistance' part - as most beings having Colossus in first place would naturally have Resistance over 5 ( they are COLOSSUS, in the end ) - so it makes being practically 'unhittable' with anything that is non-Bane. I found that much better is give beings general Armor equal to Rank, rather. It's then still hard to opposed most attacks - but not making being immune to anything less than granade launcher. Most those beings still be Rank 3-4, so they will still damn powerful to oppose most weapons damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am kind of confuse by this because that doesnt seem to be a Dread power to werewolves usual prey but for Idigam. The closest thing for &quot;normal prey&quot; (claimed, host etc) is the Armored hide (pag 216) that goes 1 to 3 and gives you that rating of armor. I kind of like your idea as a way to have a stronger armor for some of the usual prey (not Idigam).<br /> <br /> Or if you can just replicate Stalwart (193) numina that works the same but it adds to defense instead of armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:10:53-08:00","id":1168212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168197#post1168197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so if I take Living Weapon and maxed out it for Gauru claws they will have bypass 2 Armor of Colossus being, they will do +3 Damage - so it's will 'bypass' Armor 5 on hit, is it? Or will Living Weapon ***** let you automaticly bypass even Armor 10+ in Colossus beings?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you're talking about 10+ Resistance, then we are talking about Rank 4 / 5 monsters. The game is designed to make you go hunt down banes and bans for that powerful of a spirit.<br /> <br /> Lesser spirits? Well, you can try to outrank the spirit and use your claws as a bane, or just overpower the rather reasonable amount of armor. Or, don't forget Purity Rage gift. It think that's the one that gives extra damage equal to your Purity. You can easily get upwards of 6+ damage and lots of armor piercing. Or have your pack grapple the spirit, then use Killing Blow to end the battle with lots of auto-successes. Don't forget your local Storm Lord / Cahalith to also bump up your power a bit.<br /> <br /> There are seriously a ton of ways to boost damage, armor piercing, and more. And that's just for a stereotypical Rahu. Other auspieces will be using other tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-16-2017, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:23:34-08:00","id":1168215,"title":"","content":"Why on earth are you sicking a 70 corpus idigam at your players in a direct confrontation with 10+ armor and expecting them not to struggle with that proposition? Do they have 400+ xp at their disposal?<br /> <br /> I didn't went after Alduin right after Skyrim's opening sequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 12-16-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:40:53-08:00","id":1168236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168212#post1168212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lesser spirits? Well, you can try to outrank the spirit and use your claws as a bane, or just overpower the rather reasonable amount of armor. Or, don't forget Purity Rage gift. It think that's the one that gives extra damage equal to your Purity. You can easily get upwards of 6+ damage and lots of armor piercing. Or have your pack grapple the spirit, then use Killing Blow to end the battle with lots of auto-successes. Don't forget your local Storm Lord / Cahalith to also bump up your power a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Rage Gift with Purity Facet, hm?<br /> <br /> I did not know that you <i>can</i> make Killing Blow on the spirit! Would Killing Blow bypass Armor automaticlly or still need to pass this Resistance number of Damage?<br /> <br /> What do you mean about help from Storm Lord or Cahalith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:49:29-08:00","id":1168237,"title":"","content":"Cahaliths have abilities to boost your attacking power. Same with Storm Lords (at least there's the SL only rite). As for using a Killing Blow? Well, why wouldn't you be able to? Killing Blow doesn't ignore armor, but its quite common for a Rahu to have upwards of around 20+ dice. That's enough to kill most beings of low to average (1 to 3) rank. <br /> <br /> As I said before, if we're talking Rank 4 or 5 beings, then the game expects you to be hunting down the bane/ban, which completely ignores spirit armor in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T20:16:10-08:00","id":1168296,"title":"","content":"Okay, so to compile most of ways Uratha can put down high Armor enemies:<br /> 1. Outrank lesser beings, so your claws become Bane - you need only 8+ Renown dots for Rank 1 beings, 13+ Renown dots for Rank 2, and 19+ Renown dots for Rank 3.<br /> 2. <i>Living Weapon</i> Merit, which can give you Armor Piercing 2 - and in Gauru +3 Damage from claws.<br /> 3. <i>Gift's of Shaping</i> Glory Facet gives Armor Piercing equal to Glory.<br /> 4. <i>Gift's of Rage</i> Purity Facet gives extra Damage equal to Purity.<br /> 5. Possibly Killing Blow attack on spirits.<br /> 6. Cahalith or Storm Lords boosting powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Is it most of options to rise Damage and/or Armor Piercing in 2E corebook?</b> I must say it looks much more 'doable' now to have Uratha packs attack those Armor 10+ beings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T20:22:45-08:00","id":1168297,"title":"","content":"Small off-topic...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168215#post1168215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't went after Alduin right after Skyrim's opening sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you were attacked then by the <a href=\"http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Mirmulnir\" target=\"_blank\">Mirmulnir</a>, Alduin's commander - and possibly the strongest dragon to live in this times of the attack:<br /> <br /> <i>'Unlike many of the dragons who fight for <a href=\"http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Alduin\" target=\"_blank\">Alduin</a>, Mirmulnir was not raised from the dead; he has, in fact, been alive since the <a href=\"http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Merethic_Era\" target=\"_blank\">Merethic Era</a>. One of the few known hostile dragons to have survived being hunted by the Blades, he was technically one of the oldest dragons to have lived.'</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T00:46:43-08:00","id":1168328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168297#post1168297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Small off-topic...<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, you were attacked then by the <a href=\"http://&quot;http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Mirmulnir&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Mirmulnir</a>, Alduin's commander - and possibly the strongest dragon to live in this times of the attack:<br /> <br /> <i>'Unlike many of the dragons who fight for <a href=\"http://&quot;http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Alduin&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Alduin</a>, Mirmulnir was not raised from the dead; he has, in fact, been alive since the <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Merethic_Era&quot;]Merethic</a> Era[/URL]. One of the few known hostile dragons to have survived being hunted by the Blades, he was technically one of the oldest dragons to have lived.'</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so he\u2019s good at survival. Does that mean he\u2019s strong, though?<br /> <br /> Which kinda feeds back to the original topic. Yes, some beings in this game can be ludicrously powerful. At that point fighting them without specialized means is plain suicidal. Now for a reversal of perspectives. Some beings are significantly weaker than you, yet have a chance of slaughtering you. Something to keep in mind should you, in the future, have the opposite problem of the antagonist being too weak compared to your PCs. (Which honestly seems like a more probable scenario for your table- wasn\u2019t it you who were dumbfounded at your players one-shotting a major Abyssal entity in a Mage game?)<br /> <br /> Oh, and regarding Armor Piercing - wasn\u2019t there something that increased your honorary Rank on certain conditions? I remember because someone said how they noticed that even with that power Rank 7 is maximum because otherwise you\u2019d evenly match Luna, giving a theological headache. Anyways, if I\u2019m remembering correctly, that means there is indeed at least one obscure way to have your claws burn even Rank 5 beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Typo 12-17-2017, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T01:55:17-08:00","id":1168335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168296#post1168296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so to compile most of ways Uratha can put down high Armor enemies:<br /> 1. Outrank lesser beings, so your claws become Bane - you need only 8+ Renown dots for Rank 1 beings, 13+ Renown dots for Rank 2, and 19+ Renown dots for Rank 3.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a gift for raising your effective Rank by 2 while on your Territory. So, with this Gift, you easily can handle rank 1-2 beings at char gen, and rank 3 beings after a bit of time playing. There may be other ways to raise your effective rank, but I can't recall others. <br /> <br /> The only drawback here is that you have to be on your territory for it to count, but that perfectly fits with the themes of Werewolf in the first place, so that's kinda the point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. <i>Living Weapon</i> Merit, which can give you Armor Piercing 2 - and in Gauru +3 Damage from claws.<br /> 3. <i>Gift's of Shaping</i> Glory Facet gives Armor Piercing equal to Glory.<br /> 4. <i>Gift's of Rage</i> Purity Facet gives extra Damage equal to Purity.<br /> 5. Possibly Killing Blow attack on spirits.<br /> 6. Cahalith or Storm Lords boosting powers. </div> </div> </div> And don't forget Gift of Strength Purity facet. In general, a Blood Talon Rahu with decent levels of Glory and Purity is going to have easy access to a number of abilities that very significantly increase their damage. Favored Form and some other werewolf fighting merits, I'm sure, could help too. There are probably other things out there, but I can't think of any off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T01:59:04-08:00","id":1168336,"title":"","content":"Predator's Claim.<br /> <br /> 'This Facet affects an area of up to the Uratha\u2019s Purity Renown x 10 yards in radius. The Uratha\u2019s honorary Spirit Rank is increased by +2 for the purpose of attacking any spirit within the warded area. This can allow the Uratha\u2019s Spirit Rank to temporarily rise over 5, though she still cannot physically challenge spirits of Rank 6 or more.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T02:00:10-08:00","id":1168337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168328#post1168328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Something to keep in mind should you, in the future, have the opposite problem of the antagonist being too weak compared to your PCs. (Which honestly seems like a more probable scenario for your table- wasn\u2019t it you who were dumbfounded at your players one-shotting a major Abyssal entity in a Mage game?)</div> </div> </div> </div> #huntertactics<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and regarding Armor Piercing - wasn\u2019t there something that increased your honorary Rank on certain conditions? I remember because someone said how they noticed that even with that power Rank 7 is maximum because otherwise you\u2019d evenly match Luna, giving a theological headache. Anyways, if I\u2019m remembering correctly, that means there is indeed at least one obscure way to have your claws burn even Rank 5 beings. </div> </div> </div> Yep, there's a gift for that, but do note that this means that you're only able to count as a bane against up to Rank 5 beings. You'll never be able to handle Rank 6+ beings; someone of Luna's Rank that is too powerful to even create a rank 5 Royal Avatar isn't even a consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:42:30-08:00","id":1168369,"title":"","content":"So the list for high Damage against high Armor looks like this now:<br /> 1. Outrank lesser beings, so your claws become Bane - you need only 8+ Renown dots for Rank 1 beings, 13+ Renown dots for Rank 2, and 19+ Renown dots for Rank 3.<br /> 2. <i>Living Weapon</i> Merit, which can give you Armor Piercing 2 and in Gauru +3 Damage from claws.<br /> 3. <i>Gift's of Shaping</i> Glory Facet gives Armor Piercing equal to Glory.<br /> 4. <i>Gift's of Rage</i> Purity Facet gives extra Damage equal to Purity.<br /> 5. <i>Gift's of Warding </i>Purity Facet gives Honorary Rank +2 on spirits in Purity x 10 radius range.<br /> 6. <i>Gift's of Strength</i> Purity Facet adds Purity to his Strength rolls.<br /> 7. Possibly <i>Killing Blow</i> attack on spirits.<br /> 8. Cahalith or Storm Lords boosting powers.<br /> <br /> I think we have enough to make claim that high Resistance Armor can be less problem then in attack. The only real question - Is those Shadow Gifts work only on the Uratha that has them? Can they be 'cast' on pack members?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:58:20-08:00","id":1168374,"title":"","content":"Add the Symbolic Focus condition to a rank 3 Uratha with Predator's Claim and you can challenge the rank 4 abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T10:35:37-08:00","id":1168400,"title":"","content":"As has been noted in this thread as it's unfolded - high end Uratha can have a <i>very high</i> damage output. Things like Colossus give them threats that are actually meaningful, and which against high-end combat prowess is worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T11:15:18-08:00","id":1168405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168400#post1168400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been noted in this thread as it's unfolded - high end Uratha can have a <i>very high</i> damage output. Things like Colossus give them threats that are actually meaningful, and which against high-end combat prowess is worthwhile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Attack on titan with werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:08:48-08:00","id":1168894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168405#post1168405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Attack on titan with werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One of the final enemies in the closing sessions of my first full-length Forsaken chronicle in 1e was a skyscraper-sized city spirit, so... pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T13:50:44-08:00","id":1168909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168894#post1168894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One of the final enemies in the closing sessions of my first full-length Forsaken chronicle in 1e was a skyscraper-sized city spirit, so... pretty much.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I do that to my players, they whine to me for days that I try to kill them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They like it though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> I do strongly believe that an element of a story teller's creativity is the difficulties/challenges he tosses upon his players. So if something looks too strong for the players counterbalance it with a well suited scenario, or horror mood. Not all things out there are expected to be known by book readers,or to be exactly like in the book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-19-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T05:42:09-08:00","id":1169058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168894#post1168894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> One of the final enemies in the closing sessions of my first full-length Forsaken chronicle in 1e was a skyscraper-sized city spirit, so... pretty much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bane: 747 planes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T03:43:30-08:00","id":1169593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1169058#post1169058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bane: 747 planes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But they need a more specific bane, so maybe only hijacked 747 planes are it's bane...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","user":"Greyskull","date":". 12-23-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T07:49:24-08:00","id":1172256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1168909#post1168909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I do that to my players, they whine to me for days that I try to kill them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. They like it though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> I do strongly believe that an element of a story teller's creativity is the difficulties/challenges he tosses upon his players. So if something looks too strong for the players counterbalance it with a well suited scenario, or horror mood. Not all things out there are expected to be known by book readers,or to be exactly like in the book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell I certainly wasn't going soft on them; as well as the Maeljin-corrupted city spirit, there was a Bale Hound irraka with a longarm and a mad, corrupted ithalunim. To make things worse, the Bale Hound was the sole surviving member of a Pure attack that wiped out the characters' mentor pack at the beginning of the game; they'd thought he died too, only finding out he was a) still alive, b) that he was the mysterious Bale Hound causing havoc in the city all along and c) that the *entire* mentor pack had been Bale Hounds 'fighting fire with fire' against another Maeljin's influence all along - discovering all this very late in the Chronicle.<br /> <br /> That was a fun game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1169058#post1169058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bane: 747 planes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe bane was actually a purified version of an icon of authority of office. The pack had managed to get their hands on a truesilver sceptre.<br /> <br /> \u200bThey killed the city spirit by stabbing it repeatedly in one of its massive eyes of glass and cartilage with the sceptre.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd *then* they went off for a final showdown between the city's Forsaken and the invading Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T10:09:22-08:00","id":1172296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1168101-2e-fixing-dread-powers?p=1172256#post1172256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell I certainly wasn't going soft on them; as well as the Maeljin-corrupted city spirit, there was a Bale Hound irraka with a longarm and a mad, corrupted ithalunim. To make things worse, the Bale Hound was the sole surviving member of a Pure attack that wiped out the characters' mentor pack at the beginning of the game; they'd thought he died too, only finding out he was a) still alive, b) that he was the mysterious Bale Hound causing havoc in the city all along and c) that the *entire* mentor pack had been Bale Hounds 'fighting fire with fire' against another Maeljin's influence all along - discovering all this very late in the Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great scenario indeed, a pure example on how wonderful a Werewolf core campaign can be without crossover elements.<br /> Respect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}